cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "sharpFSI: a self-contained 2-D DVM + CPPC fluid-structure-interaction suite for a cycloturbine blade section"
abstract: >-
  An independent, dependency-light fluid-structure-interaction solver for a
  single cycloturbine (variable-pitch vertical-axis wind turbine) blade
  section. The fluid side is an unsteady 2-D discrete vortex method with a
  free, multiresolution vortex wake and an unsteady Kutta condition; the
  structural side is a 1-DOF rocking-pitch model with centrifugal-pendulum
  pitch control and elastic pitch stops. An optional semi-empirical
  Beddoes-Leishman-style static/dynamic-stall layer makes the solver usable in
  the deep-stall regime, and is exactly transparent in attached flow. The suite
  ships a 54-check verification harness and a head-to-head comparison against
  the independent BEM solver sharp-vawt-lab, and is intended as a
  cross-validation artefact for that code rather than as a design tool.
